  ],
  "summary": "Label numbers 1..n with Fizz, Buzz or FizzBuzz.",
  "statement": "Return a list of strings for the numbers `1` to `n`: `\"FizzBuzz\"` if the number is divisible\nby 3 and 5, `\"Fizz\"` if only by 3, `\"Buzz\"` if only by 5, otherwise the number itself as text.",
  "constraints": [
    "1 <= n <= 10^4"
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "input": "n = 5",
      "output": "[\"1\", \"2\", \"Fizz\", \"4\", \"Buzz\"]"
    },
    {
      "input": "n = 15",
      "output": "[\"1\", \"2\", \"Fizz\", \"4\", \"Buzz\", \"Fizz\", \"7\", \"8\", \"Fizz\", \"Buzz\", \"11\", \"Fizz\", \"13\", \"14\", \"FizzBuzz\"]"
    },
    {
      "input": "n = 1",
      "output": "[\"1\"]"
    }
  ],
  "signature": {
    "method": "fizzBuzz",
    "params": [
      {
        "name": "n",
        "type": "int"
      }
    ],
    "returns": "String[]"
  },
  "starter_code": "class Solution {\n    public String[] fizzBuzz(int n) {\n        // TODO: write your solution here\n        return new String[0];\n    }\n}\n",
  "hints": [
    "Which case must you check first?",
    "Check divisibility by 15 (both) before checking 3 or 5 on their own.",
    "for i in 1..n:\n    if i % 15 == 0: 'FizzBuzz'\n    elif i % 3 == 0: 'Fizz'\n    elif i % 5 == 0: 'Buzz'\n    else: str(i)",
    "One pass, O(n). The classic bug is checking 3 first, which labels 15 as just \"Fizz\"."
  ],
  "expected_complexity": {
    "time": "O(n)",
    "space": "O(n)"
  },
